A thread bound to units is not settled: it joins no queue, and starts no request on the new units.
A ready thread would never get the processor, and one moved to fewer units would keep what it saved under more;
every ready thread but the running one that may run waits on the queue its virtual time and binding say,
and one on the run queue has its request open on its payer.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a lender's virtual time comes before the release
Report: a place of a ready thread that may run waits on no queue
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -648,7 +648,6 @@ void sched_bind(struct place *p, uint32_t first, uint32_t count, uint8_t rights,
             p->vt = unit_vt[first + i];
         }
     }
-    lender_settle(place_thread(p));
 }
 
